Total miles run by each girl = $3 + 6(d-1) = 3 + 6d - 6 = 6d - 3$
Total miles run by each boy = $5(d-1) + 5 = 5d - 5 + 5 = 5d$
The coach orders the new javelins when each girl's total mileage surpasses each boy's total mileage.
So, we need to find $d$ such that $6d - 3 > 5d$.
$6d - 3 > 5d$
$6d - 5d > 3$
$d > 3$
Thus, the smallest integer $d$ such that $d > 3$ is $d=4$.
The total miles run by each girl is $6(4) - 3 = 24 - 3 = 21$ miles.
The total miles run by each boy is $5(4) = 20$ miles.
