    \multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 2x^2 & -6x & +4 \\
    \cline{4-6}
    \multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 0 & 17x & -13 \\
  \end{array}
\end{align*}

The quotient is $x^2 + 2x - 1$ and the remainder is $17x - 13$.
Calculation:
$x^4 - 3x^3 + 4x^2 + 11x - 9 = (x^2-3x+2)(x^2+ax+b) + cx+d$.
Expanding:
$x^4 - 3x^3 + 4x^2 + 11x - 9 = x^4 + ax^3 + bx^2 - 3x^3 - 3ax^2 - 3bx + 2x^2 + 2ax + 2b + cx + d$
$x^4 - 3x^3 + 4x^2 + 11x - 9 = x^4 + (a-3)x^3 + (b-3a+2)x^2 + (-3b+2a+c)x + (2b+d)$
Comparing coefficients:
$a-3 = -3 \implies a=0$
$b-3a+2 = 4 \implies b - 3(0) + 2 = 4 \implies b = 2$
$-3b+2a+c = 11 \implies -3(2)+2(0)+c = 11 \implies -6+c = 11 \implies c = 17$
$2b+d = -9 \implies 2(2)+d = -9 \implies 4+d = -9 \implies d = -13$
The remainder is $17x - 13$.

\boxed{17x-13}

